<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="PHW.D.Definitions" targetNamespace="http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/bpmn">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="PHW.D.Collaboration">
    <bpmn:participant id="PHW.D.Participant" name="D. Register a Server Client under a Data Sharing Agreement (DSA P4)" processRef="PHW.D" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="PHW.D" name="D. Register a Server Client under a Data Sharing Agreement (DSA P4)" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Registers the data recipient's server as an OAuth client of the data provider. The client is either registered dynamically (RFC 7591) or entered by an administrator. It authenticates with mutual TLS (RFC 8705) or a JWT client assertion (RFC 7523), using a key published under a trust anchor the agreement accepts, and the server records which agreement versions the client may act under. Trust-anchor neutral: WHO GDHCN is one accepted anchor among others (a national X.509 PKI, the party's own did:web, or a local list); UDAP (HL7 FAST UDAP Security) is not approved and OpenID Federation is out of scope. Source: the data sharing agreement (DSA) process analysis for litlfred/folio-assistant#2702, §2 and §4.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="PHW.D.LaneSet">
      <bpmn:lane id="PHW.Lane.DataRecipient" name="Data Recipient System (OAuth client)">
        <bpmn:documentation>The data recipient's server: the ODRL `assignee` of the agreement (ODRL 2.2 §2.1.3) and the OAuth client (RFC 6749 §1.1 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)).</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.Start</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.Gateway1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.End</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="PHW.Lane.ProviderAdmin" name="Data Provider Administrator (person)">
        <bpmn:documentation>A person at the data provider who configures systems by hand. This is the only route when the agreement is document-only (a signed PDF with no ODRL).</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="PHW.Lane.AuthorizationServer" name="Provider Authorization Server (administrator + decision point)">
        <bpmn:documentation>The provider's OAuth authorization server (RFC 6749 §1.1 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)). In NIST SP 800-207 terms it is the policy administrator. It is grouped with the policy decision point that runs process F.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="PHW.Lane.TrustAnchor" name="Trust Anchor (GDHCN or another accepted anchor)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Any trust anchor the agreement accepts. Trust-anchor neutral: WHO GDHCN is one accepted anchor among others (a national X.509 PKI, the party's own did:web, or a local list); UDAP (HL7 FAST UDAP Security) is not approved and OpenID Federation is out of scope.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>PHW.D.5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="PHW.D.Start" name="Agreement signed; recipient will call the provider&apos;s API">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: a data sharing agreement is signed, and the recipient's server will call the provider's API under it (DSA P4).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="PHW.D.1" name="D1. Prepare client key or certificate under an accepted trust anchor">
      <bpmn:documentation>The recipient uses a key pair or X.509 certificate already published under a trust anchor the agreement accepts (DSA P3). Trust-anchor neutral: WHO GDHCN is one accepted anchor among others (a national X.509 PKI, the party's own did:web, or a local list); UDAP (HL7 FAST UDAP Security) is not approved and OpenID Federation is out of scope.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="PHW.D.Gateway1" name="Registration route?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Dynamic registration (RFC 7591) or registration by an administrator. Either is valid. Only the administrator route exists for a document-only agreement.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="PHW.D.2" name="D2. Send dynamic client registration request (RFC 7591)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Client registration request (RFC 7591 §3.1 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)). For `private_key_jwt`, the metadata carries `jwks` or `jwks_uri` (RFC 7523 §2.2 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)). For mutual TLS, it carries `tls_client_auth` and the certificate subject (RFC 8705 §2.1 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)). RFC 7592 (registration management) is Experimental and needs owner approval before use.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="PHW.D.3" name="D3. Enter client by hand, scopes from the signed agreement text">
      <bpmn:documentation>Document-only route (and always allowed): the administrator registers the `client_id`, the mTLS certificate or JWKS, and scopes that match what the agreement allows. The change record cites the agreement's fixed-version URL and its SHA-256.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="PHW.D.4" name="D4. Validate client key or certificate against the accepted trust anchor">
      <bpmn:documentation>The authorization server checks that the client's key or certificate chains to, or is listed by, a trust anchor the agreement accepts: a DID document (did:web), an RFC 5280 certification path (§6 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)), or a local list.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="PHW.D.5" name="D5. Return trust list or certificate status">
      <bpmn:documentation>The trust anchor serves its signed trust list or certificate revocation list. GDHCN: `did:web:tng-cdn.who.int:v2:trustlist` with a `JsonWebSignature2020` proof. X.509: CRL (RFC 5280 §5 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="PHW.D.6" name="D6. Record which agreement versions the client may act under">
      <bpmn:documentation>The server stores, for this `client_id`, the fixed-version URL(s) of the agreement(s) it may act under. The fixed-version URL is the ODRL `uid`, the same value a client puts in RFC 9396 `identifier` (§2.2, process E). GAP: no RFC 7591 metadata field holds this, so it is the server's own configuration. No field is invented.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="PHW.D.7" name="D7. Issue client_id (RFC 7591)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Client information response with the `client_id` (RFC 7591 §3.2.1 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)), or the administrator hands it over.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="PHW.D.8" name="D8. Read authorization server metadata (RFC 8414)">
      <bpmn:documentation>The client reads the server's metadata (RFC 8414 §3 (section from standing knowledge, unverified)): token endpoint, supported client authentication methods and DPoP signing algorithms.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>PHW.D.Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="PHW.D.End" name="Client registered under the agreement">
      <bpmn:documentation>The recipient holds a `client_id` bound to its key and to the agreement version(s) recorded in D6.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>PHW.D.Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow1" sourceRef="PHW.D.Start" targetRef="PHW.D.1" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow2" sourceRef="PHW.D.1" targetRef="PHW.D.Gateway1" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow3" name="dynamic" sourceRef="PHW.D.Gateway1" targetRef="PHW.D.2" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow4" name="by administrator" sourceRef="PHW.D.Gateway1" targetRef="PHW.D.3" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow5" name="RFC 7591" sourceRef="PHW.D.2" targetRef="PHW.D.4" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow6" sourceRef="PHW.D.3" targetRef="PHW.D.4" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow7" sourceRef="PHW.D.4" targetRef="PHW.D.5" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow8" sourceRef="PHW.D.5" targetRef="PHW.D.6" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow9" sourceRef="PHW.D.6" targetRef="PHW.D.7" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow10" name="client_id" sourceRef="PHW.D.7" targetRef="PHW.D.8" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="PHW.D.Flow11" sourceRef="PHW.D.8" targetRef="PHW.D.End" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="PHW.D.Diagram">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="PHW.D.Plane" bpmnElement="PHW.D.Collaboration">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="PHW.D.Participant_di" bpmnElement="PHW.D.Participant" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="120" y="60" width="1965" height="600" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="PHW.Lane.DataRecipient_di" bpmnElement="PHW.Lane.DataRecipient" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="150" y="60" width="1935" height="150" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="PHW.Lane.ProviderAdmin_di" bpmnElement="PHW.Lane.ProviderAdmin" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="150" y="210" width="1935" height="150" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="PHW.Lane.AuthorizationServer_di" bpmnElement="PHW.Lane.AuthorizationServer" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="150" y="360" width="1935" height="150" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="PHW.Lane.TrustAnchor_di" bpmnElement="PHW.Lane.TrustAnchor" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="150" y="510" width="1935" height="150" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="PHW.D.Start_di" bpmnElement="PHW.D.Start"><dc:Bounds x="267" y="117" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
